-- title:
--   Extending an algebraic-integer point into a module-finite complete DVR
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}'$ be a commutative ring which is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, complete with respect to the adic filtration of its maximal ideal, with finite residue field and of characteristic zero, and let $p$ be a natural number whose image in $\mathcal{O}'$ lies in the maximal ideal. Let $R$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of `integralClosure ℤ ℂ`, the ring of algebraic integers inside $\mathbb{C}$, let $s$ be a finite subset of that ring, and let $\varphi : R \to \mathcal{O}'$ be a ring homomorphism. The assertion is that there exists a type $\mathcal{O}''$ carrying the structure of a commutative ring which is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, adically complete for its maximal ideal, with finite residue field and of characteristic zero, together with an $\mathcal{O}'$-algebra structure making $\mathcal{O}''$ a finite $\mathcal{O}'$-module and the structure map $\mathcal{O}' \to \mathcal{O}''$ a local homomorphism, such that the image of $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}''$, the structure map is injective, and there is a ring homomorphism $\varphi'$ from the subalgebra $R \sqcup \mathbb{Z}[s]$ generated by $R$ together with the elements of $s$ into $\mathcal{O}''$ whose restriction to $R$ (along the inclusion of $R$ into the join) is $\varphi$ followed by the structure map $\mathcal{O}' \to \mathcal{O}''$.
--
--   This is the standard device for enlarging the coefficient ring of a point of a ring of algebraic integers so as to accommodate finitely many further algebraic numbers, the enlargement being the integral closure of $\mathcal{O}'$ in a finite extension of its fraction field and hence again a complete discrete valuation ring with finite residue field, finite over $\mathcal{O}'$. It is used when passing from abstract algebraic eigenvalues of Hecke operators to coefficients in a fixed kind of coefficient ring, as in the statements about eigenforms, newforms and homomorphisms out of Hecke rings that cite it; the conclusion records the algebra structure, module-finiteness, locality and injectivity of the structure map, which a bare existence statement for a receiving discrete valuation ring would not provide.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IntegralClosure_exists_extend_ringHom_dvr_finite.lean

import Mathlib.RingTheory.DiscreteValuationRing.Basic
import Mathlib.RingTheory.AdicCompletion.Basic
import Mathlib.RingTheory.LocalRing.ResidueField.Basic
import Mathlib.RingTheory.IntegralClosure.Algebra.Basic
import Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Subalgebra.Lattice
import Mathlib.Data.Complex.Basic

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

theorem IntegralClosure.exists_extend_ringHom_dvr_finite
    {𝒪' : Type} [CommRing 𝒪'] [IsDomain 𝒪'] [IsDiscreteValuationRing 𝒪']
    [IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal 𝒪') 𝒪'] [Finite (IsLocalRing.ResidueField 𝒪')]
    [CharZero 𝒪'] {p : ℕ} (hp𝒪' : (p : 𝒪') ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal 𝒪')
    (R : Subalgebra ℤ (integralClosure ℤ ℂ)) (s : Finset (integralClosure ℤ ℂ))
    (φ : R →+* 𝒪') :
    ∃ (𝒪'' : Type) (_ : CommRing 𝒪'') (_ : IsDomain 𝒪'') (_ : IsDiscreteValuationRing 𝒪'')
      (_ : IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal 𝒪'') 𝒪'')
      (_ : Finite (IsLocalRing.ResidueField 𝒪'')) (_ : CharZero 𝒪'')
      (_ : Algebra 𝒪' 𝒪'') (_ : Module.Finite 𝒪' 𝒪'') (_ : IsLocalHom (algebraMap 𝒪' 𝒪'')),
      (p : 𝒪'') ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal 𝒪'' ∧
      Function.Injective (algebraMap 𝒪' 𝒪'') ∧
      ∃ φ' : ↥(R ⊔ Algebra.adjoin ℤ (↑s : Set (integralClosure ℤ ℂ))) →+* 𝒪'',
        ∀ x : R, φ' (Subalgebra.inclusion le_sup_left x) = algebraMap 𝒪' 𝒪'' (φ x) := by sorry
